  { sourceId: "MONDO:0013209", source: "Mondo", name: "metabolic dysfunction-associated steatotic liver disease", sourceUri: "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0013209",
    description: "Metabolic dysfunction-associated steatotic liver disease (MASLD, formerly known as nonalcoholic fatty liver disease or NAFLD) is a type of liver disease that is not caused by alcohol. It typically does not cause symptoms in the early stages, but it can cause health problems due to fat accumulation, inflammation, and scarring in the liver.",
